        "content": "     1→[\n     2→  {\n     3→    \"productName\": \"Cursor\",\n     4→    \"title\": \"Version 3.2.16: Security Review, SDK for Programmatic Agents, Canvas, Multitasking\",\n     5→    \"description\": \"April 29, 2026 release introduces Security Review beta for teams/enterprise with Security Reviewer and Vulnerability Scanner agents. Launches Cursor SDK for building programmatic agents with TypeScript. Adds Canvas for interactive visualizations, multitasking with async sub-agents, improved worktrees, and multi-root workspace support.\",\n     6→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n     7→    \"url\": \"https://cursor.com/changelog\",\n     8→    \"date\": \"2026-04-29\",\n     9→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    10→  },\n    11→  {\n    12→    \"productName\": \"Windsurf\",\n    13→    \"title\": \"Version 2.1.32: Bug Fixes & Improvements\",\n    14→    \"description\": \"April 29, 2026 release fixes crashes when switching Cascade conversations, authentication issues preventing Devin Cloud sessions from starting, and agent question response delivery problems.\",\n    15→    \"updateType\": \"bugfix\",\n    16→    \"url\": \"https://windsurf.com/changelog\",\n    17→    \"date\": \"2026-04-29\",\n    18→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    19→  },\n    20→  {\n    21→    \"productName\": \"Windsurf\",\n    22→    \"title\": \"Version 2.1.29: Devin for Terminal & Devin Agent in Windsurf\",\n    23→    \"description\": \"April 28, 2026 release introduces Devin for Terminal - a CLI agent optimized for interactive work with full codebase access. Includes seamless handoff to Devin cloud, multi-model support (Opus 4.7, GPT-5.5, SWE-1.6), and Rust-based performance. Adds Devin Local agent in Windsurf, up to 30% more token-efficient than Cascade.\",\n    24→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n    25→    \"url\": \"https://windsurf.com/changelog\",\n    26→    \"date\": \"2026-04-28\",\n    27→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    28→  },\n    29→  {\n    30→    \"productName\": \"Claude Code\",\n    31→    \"title\": \"Week 17: Ultrareview Public Preview, Session Recaps, Custom Themes\",\n    32→    \"description\": \"Claude Code Week 17 release introduces /ultrareview public research preview for cloud-based bug-hunting agents, session recaps showing activity while terminal was unfocused, custom themes system, and a redesigned web experience with sessions sidebar and drag-and-drop layout.\",\n    33→    \"updateType\": \"release\",\n    34→    \"url\": \"https://releasebot.io/updates/anthropic/claude-code\",\n    35→    \"date\": \"2026-04-27\",\n    36→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    37→  },\n    38→  {\n    39→    \"productName\": \"Windsurf\",\n    40→    \"title\": \"GPT-5.5 Available\",\n    41→    \"description\": \"April 24, 2026 announcement: GPT-5.5 model is now available in Windsurf.\",\n    42→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n    43→    \"url\": \"https://windsurf.com/changelog\",\n    44→    \"date\": \"2026-04-24\",\n    45→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    46→  },\n    47→  {\n    48→    \"productName\": \"Claude Code\",\n    49→    \"title\": \"Week 16: Opus 4.7 Default, xhigh Effort, Cloud Routines, Native CLI Binaries\",\n    50→    \"description\": \"Claude Opus 4.7 becomes default on Max and Team Premium tiers with new 'xhigh' effort level. Also introduces cloud routines for automated agents, /ultrareview parallel code review, /usage tracking, and migration to native CLI binaries for improved performance.\",\n    51→    \"updateType\": \"release\",\n    52→    \"url\": \"https://releasebot.io/updates/anthropic/claude-code\",\n    53→    \"date\": \"2026-04-20\",\n    54→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    55→  }\n    56→]\n    57→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
      }
