"header\">\n   329→        <div class=\"header-content\">\n   330→            <h1>Agentic Coding Research Report</h1>\n   331→            <span class=\"date\">May 3, 2026</span>\n   332→        </div>\n   333→    </header>\n   334→\n   335→    <div class=\"container\">\n   336→        <div class=\"stats\">\n   337→            <div class=\"stat-item\">\n   338→                <span class=\"stat-number\">16</span>\n   339→                <span class=\"stat-label\">New Products</span>\n   340→            </div>\n   341→            <div class=\"stat-item\">\n   342→                <span class=\"stat-number\">6</span>\n   343→                <span class=\"stat-label\">Product Updates</span>\n   344→            </div>\n   345→            <div class=\"stat-item\">\n   346→                <span class=\"stat-number\">13</span>\n   347→                <span class=\"stat-label\">Technical Insights</span>\n   348→            </div>\n   349→        </div>\n   350→\n   351→        <div class=\"three-column-layout\">\n   352→            <!-- New Products Section -->\n   353→            <section class=\"section new-products\">\n   354→                <h2 class=\"section-header\">New Products</h2>\n   355→\n   356→                <div class=\"item\">\n   357→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/posts/cosine-swarm\" target=\"_blank\">Cosine Swarm</a></div>\n   358→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Parallel AI agents for long-horizon, complex software tasks - uses multiple agents working in parallel on difficult coding challenges.</div>\n   359→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   360→                        <span class=\"tag\">code agent</span>\n   361→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   362→                        <span>2026-04-21</span>\n   363→                    </div>\n   364→                </div>\n   365→\n   366→                <div class=\"item\">\n   367→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/posts/gemini-deep-research-agent\" target=\"_blank\">Gemini Deep Research Agent</a></div>\n   368→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Web and MCP research agents now integrated into Gemini API for autonomous research capabilities.</div>\n   369→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   370→                        <span class=\"tag\">code agent</span>\n   371→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   372→                        <span>2026-04-30</span>\n   373→                    </div>\n   374→                </div>\n   375→\n   376→                <div class=\"item\">\n   377→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/posts/kimi-k2-6\" target=\"_blank\">Kimi K2.6</a></div>\n   378→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Open-source SOTA for long-horizon coding and agent swarms - achieves state-of-the-art performance on complex coding tasks requiring multiple steps.</div>\n   379→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   380→                        <span class=\"tag\">open-source</span>\n   381→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   382→                        <span>2026-04-21</span>\n   383→                    </div>\n   384→                </div>\n   385→\n   386→                <div class=\"item\">\n   387→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/posts/chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicle</a></div>\n   388→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Build Codex memories from recent screen context - provides persistent memory for AI coding agents from screen activity.</div>\n   389→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   390→                        <span class=\"tag\">code agent</span>\n   391→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   392→                        <span>2026-04-21</span>\n   393→                    </div>\n   394→                </div>\n   395→\n   396→                <div class=\"item\">\n   397→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/wuphf-2\" target=\"_blank\">WUPHF by Nex.ai</a></div>\n   398→                    <div class=\"item-description\">A collaborative office of AI employees who build and maintain their own knowledge base to never lose context for tasks. Compatible with Claude Code, Codexes, and OpenClaude agents.</div>\n   399→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Slack for AI employees with a shared brain\"</div>\n   400→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   401→                        <span class=\"tag\">code agent</span>\n   402→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   403→                        <span>2026-04-28</span>\n   404→                    </div>\n   405→                </div>\n   406→\n   407→                <div class=\"item\">\n   408→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/posts/tabstack\" target=\"_blank\">Tabstack</a></div>\n   409→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Extract web data and automate browsers without requiring scrapers. API for browser automation.</div>\n   410→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   411→                        <span class=\"tag\">workflow agent</span>\n   412→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   413→                        <span>2026-04-30</span>\n   414→                    </div>\n   415→                </div>\n   416→\n   417→                <div class=\"item\">\n   418→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/posts/mintlify-editor\" target=\"_blank\">Mintlify Editor</a></div>\n   419→                    <div class=\"item-description\">AI-native collaborative editor for documentation with GitHub integration. Allows publishing customer-facing docs directly.</div>\n   420→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"The ability to publish customer facing docs is just amazing\"</div>\n   421→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   422→                        <span class=\"tag\">IDE-integrated</span>\n   423→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   424→                        <span>2026-04-30</span>\n   425→                    </div>\n   426→                </div>\n   427→\n   428→                <div class=\"item\">\n   429→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/posts/rova-ai\" target=\"_blank\">Rova AI</a></div>\n   430→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Autonomous, goal-driven testing for web and mobile apps - AI agent for automated QA testing.</div>\n   431→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   432→                        <span class=\"tag\">workflow agent</span>\n   433→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   434→                        <span>2026-04-30</span>\n   435→                    </div>\n   436→                </div>\n   437→\n   438→                <div class=\"item\">\n   439→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/posts/symphony\" target=\"_blank\">Symphony</a></div>\n   440→                    <div class=\"item-description\">An open-source specification for Codex orchestration - provides standards for coordinating AI coding agents.</div>\n   441→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   442→                        <span class=\"tag\">workflow agent</span>\n   443→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   444→                        <span>2026-04-30</span>\n   445→                    </div>\n   446→                </div>\n   447→\n   448→                <div class=\"item\">\n   449→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/posts/mistral-medium-3-5\" target=\"_blank\">Mistral Medium 3.5</a></div>\n   450→                    <div class=\"item-description\">A 128B model for coding, reasoning, and long tasks - optimized for software development and complex reasoning tasks.</div>\n   451→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   452→                        <span class=\"tag\">code agent</span>\n   453→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   454→                        <span>2026-04-30</span>\n   455→                    </div>\n   456→                </div>\n   457→\n   458→                <div class=\"item\">\n   459→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/posts/spectrum\" target=\"_blank\">Spectrum</a></div>\n   460→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Bring agents to all the interfaces people already use - open-source tool for integrating AI agents into existing messaging platforms.</div>\n   461→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   462→                        <span class=\"tag\">open-source</span>\n   463→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   464→                        <span>2026-04-21</span>\n   465→                    </div>\n   466→                </div>\n   467→\n   468→                <div class=\"item\">\n   469→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/posts/basedash-dashboard-agent\" target=\"_blank\">Basedash Dashboard Agent</a></div>\n   470→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Builds entire dashboards from a single prompt - AI agent for dashboard and analytics creation.</div>\n   471→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   472→                        <span class=\"tag\">workflow agent</span>\n   473→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   474→                        <span>2026-04-30</span>\n   475→                    </div>\n   476→                </div>\n   477→\n   478→                <div class=\"item\">\n   479→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/posts/blueprint\" target=\"_blank\">Blueprint</a></div>\n   480→                    <div class=\"item-description\">One-shot bigger coding tasks - an AI tool that handles larger coding tasks in a single operation.</div>\n   481→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   482→                        <span class=\"tag\">code agent</span>\n   483→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   484→                        <span>2026-04-28</span>\n   485→                    </div>\n   486→                </div>\n   487→\n   488→                <div class=\"item\">\n   489→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/posts/x-island\" target=\"_blank\">X Island</a></div>\n   490→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Dynamic Island for AI Coding Agents - provides a compact UI for monitoring AI coding agent activity.</div>\n   491→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   492→                        <span class=\"tag\">IDE-integrated</span>\n   493→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   494→                        <span>2026-04-21</span>\n   495→                    </div>\n   496→                </div>\n   497→\n   498→                <div class=\"item\">\n   499→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/posts/jitera\" target=\"_blank\">Jitera</a></div>\n   500→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Shared context that turns AI into your teammate - provides persistent context for AI collaboration.</div>\n   501→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   502→                        <span class=\"tag\">workflow agent</span>\n   503→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   504→                        <span>2026-04-28</span>\n   505→                    </div>\n   506→                </div>\n   507→\n   508→                <div class=\"item\">\n   509→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/posts/twenty-2-0\" target=\"_blank\">Twenty 2.0</a></div>\n   510→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Build your Enterprise CRM with an AI-friendly SDK - developer tools for building CRM systems with native AI integration.</div>\n   511→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   512→                        <span class=\"tag\">workflow agent</span>\n   513→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   514→                        <span>2026-04-21</span>\n   515→                    </div>\n   516→                </div>\n   517→\n   518→                <div class=\"item\">\n   519→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/posts/pioneer\" target=\"_blank\">Pioneer</a></div>\n   520→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Fine-tune any LLM in minutes with one prompt - developer tool for quickly customizing language models.</div>\n   521→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   522→                        <span class=\"tag\">workflow agent</span>\n   523→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   524→                        <span>2026-04-21</span>\n   525→                    </div>\n   526→                </div>\n   527→            </section>\n   528→\n   529→            <!-- Whitelist Updates Section -->\n   530→            <section class=\"section whitelist-updates\">\n   531→                <h2 class=\"section-header\">Product Updates</h2>\n   532→\n   533→                <div class=\"item\">\n   534→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://windsurf.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Windsurf v2.1.32: Bug Fixes & Improvements</a></div>\n   535→                    <div class=\"item-description\">April 29, 2026 release fixes crashes when switching Cascade conversations, authentication issues preventing Devin Cloud sessions from starting, and agent question response delivery problems.</div>\n   536→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   537→                        <span class=\"update-type bugfix\">bugfix</span>\n   538→                        <span class=\"source\">2026-04-29</span>\n   539→                    </div>\n   540→                </div>\n   541→\n   542→                <div class=\"item\">\n   543→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://windsurf.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Windsurf v2.1.29: Devin for Terminal</a></div>\n   544→                    <div class=\"item-description\">April 28, 2026 release introduces Devin for Terminal - a CLI agent optimized for interactive work with full codebase access. Includes seamless handoff to Devin cloud, multi-model support (Opus 4.7, GPT-5.5, SWE-1.6), and Rust-based performance.</div>\n   545→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   546→                        <span class=\"update-type feature\">feature</span>\n   547→                        <span class=\"source\">2026-04-28</span>\n   548→                    </div>\n   549→                </div>\n   550→\n   551→                <div class=\"item\">\n   552→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://windsurf.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Windsurf: GPT-5.5 Available</a></div>\n   553→                    <div class=\"item-description\">April 24, 2026 announcement: GPT-5.5 model is now available in Windsurf.</div>\n   554→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   555→                        <span class=\"update-type feature\">feature</span>\n   556→                        <span class=\"source\">2026-04-24</span>\n   557→                    </div>\n   558→                </div>\n   559→\n   560→                <div class=\"item\">\n   561→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Cursor v3.2.16: Security Review, SDK, Canvas</a></div>\n   562→                    <div class=\"item-description\">April 29, 2026 release introduces Security Review beta for teams/enterprise, Cursor SDK for building programmatic agents with TypeScript, Canvas for interactive visualizations, multitasking with async sub-agents, improved worktrees, and multi-root workspace support.</div>\n   563→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   564→                        <span class=\"update-type feature\">feature</span>\n   565→                        <span class=\"source\">2026-04-29</span>\n   566→                    </div>\n   567→                </div>\n   568→\n   569→                <div class=\"item\">\n   570→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://releasebot.io/updates/anthropic/claude-code\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code Week 17: Ultrareview, Themes</a></div>\n   571→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Claude Code Week 17 release introduces /ultrareview public research preview for cloud-based bug-hunting agents, session recaps showing activity while terminal was unfocused, custom themes system, and redesigned web experience with sessions sidebar.</div>\n   572→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   573→                        <span class=\"update-type release\">release</span>\n   574→                        <span class=\"source\">2026-04-27</span>\n   575→                    </div>\n   576→                </div>\n   577→\n   578→                <div class=\"item\">\n   579→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://releasebot.io/updates/anthropic/claude-code\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code Week 16: Opus 4.7, Routines</a></div>\n   580→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Claude Opus 4.7 becomes default on Max and Team Premium tiers with new 'xhigh' effort level. Also introduces cloud routines for automated agents, /ultrareview parallel code review, /usage tracking, and migration to native CLI binaries.</div>\n   581→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   582→                        <span class=\"update-type release\">release</span>\n   583→                        <span class=\"source\">2026-04-20</span>\n   584→                    </div>\n   585→                </div>\n   586→            </section>\n   587→\n   588→            <!-- Technical Insights Section -->\n   589→            <section class=\"section technical-insights\">\n   590→                <h2 class=\"section-header\">Technical Insights</h2>\n   591→\n   592→                <div class=\"item\">\n   593→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   594→                        <span class=\"insight-type technical\">technical</span>\n   595→                        <span class=\"source\">Flue Team</span>\n   596→                    </div>\n   597→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://flueframework.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Flue - Agent Harness Framework for TypeScript</a></div>\n   598→                    <div class=\"item-description\">TypeScript framework for building autonomous agents with Agent = Model + Harness architecture. Features skills as reusable workflows, session management, fine-grained token control, and multiple sandbox support including virtual, Daytona containers, and Cloudflare Workers.</div>\n   599→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   600→                        <span class=\"topic\">agents</span>\n   601→                        <span class=\"topic\">TypeScript</span>\n   602→                        <span class=\"topic\">agent harness</span>\n   603→                        <span class=\"topic\">sandboxes</span>\n   604→                        <span class=\"topic\">Claude</span>\n   605→                    </div>\n   606→                </div>\n   607→\n   608→                <div class=\"item\">\n   609→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   610→                        <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">opinion</span>\n   611→                        <span class=\"source\">Mendral</span>\n   612→                    </div>\n   613→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.mendral.com/blog/agent-harness-belongs-outside-sandbox\" target=\"_blank\">The Agent Harness Belongs Outside the Sandbox</a></div>\n   614→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Argues agent harnesses should run outside the sandbox for better credential security, cost savings (suspend idle sandboxes), and multi-user support. Architecture enables durable execution with Inngest and filesystem virtualization.</div>\n   615→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   616→                        <span class=\"topic\">agent architecture</span>\n   617→                        <span class=\"topic\">sandboxes</span>\n   618→                        <span class=\"topic\">security</span>\n   619→                        <span class=\"topic\">multi-user agents</span>\n   620→                    </div>\n   621→                </div>\n   622→\n   623→                <div class=\"item\">\n   624→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   625→                        <span class=\"insight-type discussion\">discussion</span>\n   626→                        <span class=\"source\">Microsoft VS Code Team</span>\n   627→                    </div>\n   628→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/pull/310226\" target=\"_blank\">VS Code inserting 'Co-Authored-by Copilot' into commits</a></div>\n   629→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Microsoft changed git.addAICoAuthor default from 'off' to 'all', automatically adding Copilot co-authorship to commits. Community backlash: 129 thumbs down. Users call it 'vandalism' and question Copilot adoption metrics.</div>\n   630→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   631→                        <span class=\"topic\">VS Code</span>\n   632→                        <span class=\"topic\">GitHub Copilot</span>\n   633→                        <span class=\"topic\">Git</span>\n   634→                        <span class=\"topic\">AI attribution</span>\n   635→                    </div>\n   636→                </div>\n   637→\n   638→                <div class=\"item\">\n   639→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   640→                        <span class=\"insight-type article\">article</span>\n   641→                        <span class=\"source\">TechCrunch</span>\n   642→                    </div>\n   643→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/02/the-best-ai-powered-dictation-apps-of-2025/\" target=\"_blank\">Best AI dictation apps, tested and ranked</a></div>\n   644→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Comprehensive review of AI-powered dictation apps: Wispr Flow, Willow, Monologue, Superwhisper, VoiceTypr, Aqua, Typeless, Dictato. Pricing varies from $8-15/month subscriptions to $35-100+ lifetime licenses. Useful for 'even coding through your voice' with IDE integration.</div>\n   645→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   646→                        <span class=\"topic\">voice AI</span>\n   647→                        <span class=\"topic\">dictation</span>\n   648→                        <span class=\"topic\">speech-to-text</span>\n   649→                        <span class=\"topic\">productivity</span>\n   650→                    </div>\n   651→                </div>\n   652→\n   653→                <div class=\"item\">\n   654→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   655→                        <span class=\"insight-type discussion\">discussion</span>\n   656→                        <span class=\"source\">Hacker News Community</span>\n   657→                    </div>\n   658→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://hnup.date/hn-sota\" target=\"_blank\">SOTA Coding Models According to HN</a></div>\n   659→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Hacker News discussion aggregating community opinions on state-of-the-art coding models based on commenter experiences and benchmarks. Covers various models' performance on coding tasks with real-world usage patterns.</div>\n   660→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   661→                        <span class=\"topic\">coding models</span>\n   662→                        <span class=\"topic\">LLMs</span>\n   663→                        <span class=\"topic\">benchmarks</span>\n   664→                        <span class=\"topic\">community</span>\n   665→                    </div>\n   666→                </div>\n   667→\n   668→                <div class=\"item\">\n   669→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   670→                        <span class=\"insight-type news\">news</span>\n   671→                        <span class=\"source\">MIT Technology Review</span>\n   672→                    </div>\n   673→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.technologyreview.com/2026/05/01/1136800/musk-v-altman-week-1-musk-says-he-was-duped-warns-ai-could-kill-us-all-and-admits-that-xai-distills-openais-models/\" target=\"_blank\">Musk v. Altman: Week 1 Trial Highlights</a></div>\n   674→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Week 1 of Musk vs OpenAI trial: Musk testified he was 'a fool who provided them free funding' of $38M. Admitted xAI 'partly' distills OpenAI's models - using OpenAI's technology to train Grok, causing gasps in courtroom. Trial outcome could upend OpenAI's path to $1T IPO.</div>\n   675→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   676→                        <span class=\"topic\">OpenAI</span>\n   677→                        <span class=\"topic\">Elon Musk</span>\n   678→                        <span class=\"topic\">xAI</span>\n   679→                        <span class=\"topic\">Sam Altman</span>\n   680→                        <span class=\"topic\">lawsuit</span>\n   681→                    </div>\n   682→                </div>\n   683→\n   684→                <div class=\"item\">\n   685→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   686→                        <span class=\"insight-type news\">news</span>\n   687→                        <span class=\"source\">Wired</span>\n   688→                    </div>\n   689→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.wired.com/story/openai-enables-cookies-by-default-for-free-chatgpt-users/\" target=\"_blank\">OpenAI Enables Marketing Cookies by Default</a></div>\n   690→                    <div class=\"item-description\">OpenAI updated privacy policy to enable marketing cookies by default for free ChatGPT users in US. Shares limited identifiers (email, cookie IDs, device IDs) with advertising partners to track ad conversions. Users can opt out via Settings.</div>\n   691→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   692→                        <span class=\"topic\">OpenAI</span>\n   693→                        <span class=\"topic\">ChatGPT</span>\n   694→                        <span class=\"topic\">privacy</span>\n   695→                        <span class=\"topic\">cookies</span>\n   696→                        <span class=\"topic\">tracking</span>\n   697→                    </div>\n   698→                </div>\n   699→\n   700→                <div class=\"item\">\n   701→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   702→                        <span class=\"insight-type news\">news</span>\n   703→                        <span class=\"source\">TechCrunch</span>\n   704→                    </div>\n   705→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/01/meta-buys-robotics-startup-to-bolster-its-humanoid-ai-ambitions/\" target=\"_blank\">Meta buys robotics startup for humanoid AI</a></div>\n   706→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Meta acquired humanoid robotics startup Assured Robot Intelligence (ARI). Team joins Meta's Superintelligence Labs. Reflects Meta's long-term humanoid robotics ambitions. Follows Amazon's acquisition of Fauna Robotics last month.</div>\n   707→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   708→                        <span class=\"topic\">Meta</span>\n   709→                        <span class=\"topic\">robotics</span>\n   710→                        <span class=\"topic\">humanoid robots</span>\n   711→                        <span class=\"topic\">acquisitions</span>\n   712→                        <span class=\"topic\">AGI</span>\n   713→                    </div>\n   714→                </div>\n   715→\n   716→                <div class=\"item\">\n   717→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   718→                        <span class=\"insight-type technical\">technical</span>\n   719→                        <span class=\"source\">MIT Technology Review</span>\n   720→                    </div>\n   721→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.technologyreview.com/2026/04/30/1136721/this-startups-new-mechanistic-interpretability-tool-lets-you-debug-llms/\" target=\"_blank\">Goodfire's Silico: LLM Debugging Tool</a></div>\n   722→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Mechanistic interpretability tool for debugging and tweaking LLMs by examining individual neurons and pathways. Features: zoom into specific neurons, run experiments, trace pathways, adjust parameters, filter training data. Found 'trolley problem' neuron in Qwen 3.</div>\n   723→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   724→                        <span class=\"topic\">mechanistic interpretability</span>\n   725→                        <span class=\"topic\">LLM debugging</span>\n   726→                        <span class=\"topic\">Goodfire</span>\n   727→                        <span class=\"topic\">AI safety</span>\n   728→                    </div>\n   729→                </div>\n   730→\n   731→                <div class=\"item\">\n   732→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   733→                        <span class=\"insight-type technical\">technical</span>\n   734→                        <span class=\"source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   735→                    </div>\n   736→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex/releases/tag/rust-v0.128.0\" target=\"_blank\">Codex CLI 0.128.0 adds /goal feature</a></div>\n   737→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Introduces /goal feature similar to Ralph loop pattern. Users set a goal and Codex loops until goal is completed or token budget exhausted. Implemented through prompts automatically injected at end of each turn for autonomous iterative problem-solving.</div>\n   738→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   739→                        <span class=\"topic\">Codex CLI</span>\n   740→                        <span class=\"topic\">OpenAI</span>\n   741→                        <span class=\"topic\">coding agents</span>\n   742→                        <span class=\"topic\">autonomous coding</span>\n   743→                    </div>\n   744→                </div>\n   745→\n   746→                <div class=\"item\">\n   747→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   748→                        <span class=\"insight-type technical\">technical</span>\n   749→                        <span class=\"source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   750→                    </div>\n   751→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/29/llm/\" target=\"_blank\">LLM 0.32a0: Major Refactor</a></div>\n   752→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Major alpha release of LLM Python library. Model inputs now represented as sequence of messages. Responses can be streams of differently typed parts (text, tool calls, reasoning, images, audio). Supports streaming typed message parts for modern frontier models.</div>\n   753→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   754→                        <span class=\"topic\">LLM</span>\n   755→                        <span class=\"topic\">Python</span>\n   756→                        <span class=\"topic\">CLI tools</span>\n   757→                        <span class=\"topic\">streaming</span>\n   758→                        <span class=\"topic\">multi-modal</span>\n   759→                    </div>\n   760→                </div>\n   761→\n   762→                <div class=\"item\">\n   763→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   764→                        <span class=\"insight-type technical\">technical</span>\n   765→                        <span class=\"source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   766→                    </div>\n   767→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/microsoft/VibeVoice\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft VibeVoice - Whisper-style audio model</a></div>\n   768→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Whisper-style audio model for speech-to-text with speaker diarization built in. MIT licensed. Model is 17.3GB, with 4-bit quantized version at 5.71GB. Can run on Apple Silicon using mlx-audio with simple one-liner command.</div>\n   769→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   770→                        <span class=\"topic\">speech-to-text</span>\n   771→                        <span class=\"topic\">audio models</span>\n   772→                        <span class=\"topic\">Microsoft</span>\n   773→                        <span class=\"topic\">local models</span>\n   774→                    </div>\n   775→                </div>\n   776→\n   777→                <div class=\"item\">\n   778→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   779→                        <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">opinion</span>\n   780→                        <span class=\"source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   781→                    </div>\n   782→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/27/now-deceased-agi-clause/\" target=\"_blank\">History of OpenAI-Microsoft AGI Clause</a></div>\n   783→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Documents the death of the unusual AGI clause in Microsoft-OpenAI partnership. Originally stated Microsoft's commercial IP rights would end upon AGI achievement. As of April 27, 2026, new agreement states license continues through 2032 'independent of OpenAI's technology progress'.</div>\n   784→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   785→                        <span class=\"topic\">OpenAI</span>\n   786→                        <span class=\"topic\">Microsoft</span>\n   787→                        <span class=\"topic\">AGI</span>\n   788→                        <span class=\"topic\">partnerships</span>\n   789→                        <span class=\"topic\">licensing</span>\n   790→                    </div>\n   791→                </div>\n   792→            </section>\n   793→        </div>\n   794→    </div>\n   795→\n   796→    <footer class=\"footer\">\n   797→        <div class=\"footer-content\">\n   798→            <div class=\"footer-links\">\n   799→                <a href=\"#\">Archive</a>\n   800→                <a href=\"#\">About</a>\n   801→                <a href=\"#\">RSS Feed</a>\n   802→                <a href=\"#\">Source Code</a>\n   803→            </div>\n   804→            <p style=\"margin-top: 10px; font-size: 11px; color: #828282;\">\n   805→                Generated with Claude Code • Data compiled from Product Hunt, GitHub, Hacker News, and tech publications\n   806→            </p>\n   807→        </div>\n   808→    </footer>\n   809→</body>\n   810→</html>\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
